  "facts": [
    "The New Yalu River Bridge, a 3‑kilometer cable‑stayed marvel, began construction in October 2011, cost China US$350 million, and was designed to replace the single‑track Sino‑Korean Friendship Bridge.",
    "Construction stalled between 2014 and 2019, leaving the North Korean side unfinished; by 2021, work on that side was largely complete, and the bridge was poised to open soon.",
    "In June 2019, Xi Jinping pledged to fund roads and customs posts on the North Korean side, and by October 2021 the ramps were finished, with a customs and immigration center resuming work in February 2025."
  ],
